{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He will judge</b> — the word אשר is missing, like (1 Chronicles 12:38) עם לבבך שלם. And thus it is: <b>He will judge among the nations</b> — who is full of bodies, that he has a great army; he will execute judgment among the nations." "<b>Over a great land</b> — which is not called an island, and it is the land of Israel, and Media, and Persia. And Rabbi Moses [ibn Janah] said: the meaning is great, son of Ammon."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 110, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes עם לבבכם שלם but the phrase appears in 1 Chronicles 12:39 (12:38 in some numbering) as עם שלם לבבו; resolved to 1 Chronicles 12:38 following the citation as given.", 1 "Reading רבה as 'great' on the surface level; Rabbi Moses's interpretation apparently parses it differently, possibly as a toponym. The phrase רבת בני עמון is rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:24.789720546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}